
S203  page=roo.html  claimed-anchor='What Skills Let You Do'
  block 68: chain = 'Skills > What Skills Let You Do\u200b'
    claimed anchor present in chain: True
    block text: Override Control: Project skills override global skills, mode-specific override generic

S204  page=amp.html  claimed-anchor='Skill Sources and Precedence'
  block 109: chain = 'Skills > Skill Sources and Precedence'
    claimed anchor present in chain: True
    block text: Local skills mask repository skills with the same name. A personal skill masks a workspace skill with the same name, and both mask official Amp skills. Set amp.skills.disableClaudeCodeSkills in Configuration to skip the Claude-compatible locations, or amp.skills.disableGlobalAgentsSkills to skip ~/.config/agents/skills/ and ~/.agents/skills/.

S205  page=deep.html  claimed-anchor='Scan Locations'
  block 34: chain = 'Agent Skills > Scan Locations'
    claimed anchor present in chain: True
    block text: Deep Code scans skills in the following order. If multiple skills resolve to the same name, only the highest-priority one is kept.

S206  page=junie.html  claimed-anchor='Skill location'
  block 55: chain = 'Agent skills > How Junie CLI uses skills > Skill location'
    claimed anchor present in chain: True
    block text: If a project-level (<projectRoot>/.junie/skills/<skill-name>/) and a user-level (~/.junie/skills/<skill-name>/) skills share the same name, the project-level skill takes precedence and the user-level skill is ignored.

S207  page=opencode.html  claimed-anchor='Troubleshoot loading'
  block 210: chain = 'Agent Skills > Troubleshoot loading'
    claimed anchor present in chain: True
    block text: Ensure skill names are unique across all locations

S208  page=ms.html  claimed-anchor='Tool approval'
  block 84: chain = 'Agent Skills > Use Agent Skills with Harness Agent'
    claimed anchor present in chain: False
    block text: All three skill tools require approval by default. The harness tool-approval middleware is enabled by default, but its default options don't auto-approve any tool. Use AgentSkillsProvider.ReadOnlyToolsAutoApprovalRule or AgentSkillsProvider.AllToolsAutoApprovalRule only for skill sources you trust.
  block 89: chain = 'Agent Skills > Use Agent Skills with Harness Agent'
    claimed anchor present in chain: False
    block text: All three skill tools require approval by default. Because the harness installs ToolApprovalMiddleware by default, pass a session on every run and use auto_approval_rules for trusted read-only or all-tool approval policies.

S201  page=ms.html  claimed-anchor='Security best practices'
  block 528: chain = 'Agent Skills > Security best practices'
    claimed anchor present in chain: True
    block text: Agent Skills should be treated like any third-party code you bring into your project.Because skill instructions are injected into the agent's context - and skills can include scripts - applying the same level of review and governance you would to an open-source dependency is essential.
